sins. Both have access to different realms, and the Brood might surprise the Forsaken by following them into the Shadow. On the other hand, following the Begotten into their Lair might prove hard for the Forsaken, and an ambush from the Primordeal Realm would be an effective strategy - which loses in effectiveness the more the Forsaken have learned. Their family-sensing abilities might thwart attempts to scout out in human or wolf-form by an incautious Pack, but it is more likely they will at least expend the effort to stay hidden, possibly forcing a Clash of Wills. However, going Garou is a gamechanger, and forces unprepared Begotten to spend Satiety to cause meaningful harm.<br /> If the Brood gets to start the war, edged on by Hosts maybe, they could expend time on learning more about the Uratha and are likely to make use of silver, however, I'd peck their advantage gain as lower than Wolves that go full on Siskur-Dah.<br /> <br /> Which abilities and traits would help the Begotten survive or even take such a fight, though? In my opinion, one of the most valuable abilities would be the Lair Trait Rotting: reducing their regenerative capabilities is taking away one of the Uratha's greatest boons - especially in Garou. Stench and Thunderous are two additional Traits that would seriously hamper the Forsaken. Thin Air and Heavy seem also useful in disencouraging the use of Dalu, Garou etc. Suffocating or Noxious Gas might help a lot, too, and Slick or Cramped would also be very useful.<br /> An anti-Werewolf Begotten would probably have Razored Silver in his Lair, but that would be incredibly specific.<br /> Limb from Limb is an obvious Atavism here, as is Unbreakable and Relentless Hunter. Looming Presence might be of surprisingly good use, not just due to the health increase, but the Rote quality for Intimidation.<br /> If the Brood is more likely to try and find a trade-off, Alien Allure and Siren's Treacherous Song could find great application. The latter might also help in disrupting a pack's team work a bit, by Deafening them, which might be a nice set-up for an ambush.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sensory deprivation that doesn't simultaneously target all senses on Uratha is useless as the other senses instantly compensate for the missing one(s), thus the deprived sense affords the werewolf no penalty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12191,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","user":"Malus","date":". 08-24-2017, 01:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T10:54:50-07:00","id":1133456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1133403-fighting-among-family-beasts-vs-other-splats?p=1133445#post1133445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sensory deprivation that doesn't simultaneously target all senses on Uratha is useless as the other senses instantly compensate for the missing one(s), thus the deprived sense affords the werewolf no penalty.</div> </div> </div> </div>Stench Does Not deprive, Neither Does Thunderous. They outright attack the senses through overstimulation, even temporarily Damaging respective organs in the case of thunderous.<br /> I have not come across anything that says &quot;Uratha can willfully deactivate one sense&quot;? Might be an oversight, though.<br /> Still, using stench, Thunderous and throwing in darkness doesn't leave them much to go on","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T11:03:03-07:00","id":1133460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1133403-fighting-among-family-beasts-vs-other-splats?p=1133456#post1133456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Stench Does Not deprive, Neither Does Thunderous. They outright attack the senses through overstimulation, even temporarily Damaging respective organs in the case of thunderous.<br /> I have not come across anything that says &quot;Uratha can willfully deactivate one sense&quot;? Might be an oversight, though.<br /> Still, using stench, Thunderous and throwing in darkness doesn't leave them much to go on</div> </div> </div> </div>Lemme find the quote for you:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Further, if she would normally suffer penalties due to deprivation (blindness,<br /> strong scents, or deafness), her other senses compensate, negating those penalties entirely. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T11:54:59-07:00","id":1133481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1133403-fighting-among-family-beasts-vs-other-splats?p=1133460#post1133460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lemme find the quote for you:</div> </div> </div> </div>Using wolf senses \u2014 which is what that line is talking about \u2014 requires a conscious action in non-wolf forms and by context does nothing to mitigate penalties to non-Perception rolls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T12:10:07-07:00","id":1133489,"title":"","content":"Interested in fansplats Wormwood?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T12:20:34-07:00","id":1133493,"title":"","content":"Beasts effectively personify the core antagonist splat for every game line, which is a big reason for them to be enemies. They preach the word of the strix, the Pure and hosts, and the seers and scelesti. They are more likely to see centimani, huntsmen and Gentry as potential friends and 'regular' prometheans and changelings as obstructionist. You really don't need much of a stretch when coming up with reasons for them to not get along.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1133403-fighting-among-family-beasts-vs-other-splats?p=1133481#post1133481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Using wolf senses \u2014 which is what that line is talking about \u2014 requires a conscious action in non-wolf forms and by context does nothing to mitigate penalties to non-Perception rolls.</div> </div> </div> </div>Despite it's location, that quote isn't talking about wolf senses. You can ask the developer if you believe otherwise.<br /> <br /> Wormwood is right, though, those Lair Traits don't work on depriving senses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-24-2017, 03:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T12:50:44-07:00","id":1133511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1133403-fighting-among-family-beasts-vs-other-splats?p=1133481#post1133481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Using wolf senses \u2014 which is what that line is talking about \u2014 requires a conscious action in non-wolf forms and by context does nothing to mitigate penalties to non-Perception rolls.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is a reflexive (ie, instantaneous) action.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar886_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"886\" data-vbnamecard=\"886\">nofather</a> deprivation (blindness,strong scents, or deafness), Stench counts as strong scent; same with Thunderous; in fact, being things that have an effective hearing range of 1 mile per primal urge, they would react like someone on the autistic spectrum to stimuli, yet they can process city noise without penalties at sound frequencies way below human hearing; and Rotting says nothing about regeneration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12191,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","user":"Malus","date":". 08-24-2017, 04:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T13:21:03-07:00","id":1133527,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar134_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"134\" data-vbnamecard=\"134\">The Kings Raven</a> sure, hit me up! Just be sure to give a little additional information, as fansplats' abilities are usually not as well known (e.g. to me) =)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar886_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"886\" data-vbnamecard=\"886\">nofather</a> True enough, I still thought it might be interesting to develop those things a bit outside the obvious. However, I admit to not having thought about it that way - thanks for that juicy morsel of &quot;preach the word of the strix&quot;: that's gonna find use quite soon in a vamp plot hook =D<br /> <br /> Rereading the quote, I might actually agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12191_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12191\" data-vbnamecard=\"12191\">Malus</a> : while it says &quot;depriving senses&quot;, the text lists <b>strong scents</b> and <b>deafening </b>as examples, in which case the 'depriving' might actually have to be attributed to &quot;the sense is being taken out&quot;. Huh. A bit overpowered, if taking out two senses is not enough to inflict a penalty, imo. But then, there are other ways to do so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T14:33:45-07:00","id":1133549,"title":"","content":"If you build a combat monster out of a Rahu Blood Talon and an Anakim Nemesis with 0xp, and focus purely on the physical encounter in a purely white room scenario, you'll still have to question the aspect of effective range, mobility, and DPR, and survivability. Now you know the most effective way to handle a werewolf is silver, but you don't have reliable built in access to silver as a beast. You do, however, have access to Aggravated Damage from two atavisms, Limb from Limb and Dragonfire. The most effective weapon against beasts is Hero's ability to put a bane on you, so the wolf has no access to that. He does, however, have the ability to literally eat the beast for Aggravated damage.<br /> <br /> The Beast has access to at least one form of regeneration that can even regen ag, and one form of armor against even ag damage- this time I suggest the latter, to turn werewolf damage into chip damage. Looming Presence, especially in conjunction with Advanced Giant, will help reduce the wolf's attack pool. There werewolves have constant slow regen, and if they are willing to Death Rage, they have access to a boatload of regen.<br /> <br /> The real answer to this fight is going to be the beast getting the werewolf to rage early, then CCing him down somehow. And that's where the beasts' last big ability come's in- the Lair. Extreme Heat can force the wolf into War Form to survive, while Engulfing will help keep him snared. To build the Anakim to fight a wolf, I'm suggesting Looming Presence and Dragonfire, to reduce the wolf's ability to hit, and provide yourself some good offense, as well as Extreme Heat and Engulfing. Run Away and You Must Obey are your best starting nightmares here- primarily because they aren't stamina primary, and we've build two deliberately combat focused characters. Tactics: Use the dragonfire to bring the heat, call down the engulfing trait. Looming Presence can give you extra movement speed to stay ahead even if the engulfing fails at some point.<br /> <br /> For the Rahu, I'd probably take Slaughterer and Primal Strength myself. (Note: both are Purity Renown). That gives you some good offense, and with Killer Instinct and Warrior's Hide to help bump your hp. Your built in survivability and DPR are pretty good, and your powers and rahu nature bump that up to a solid rating. You have to worry about the Basu-Im timer, so you're best tactic is to mix it up close and personal with Urhan/Urshul, then Garu and eat the Begotten- literally.<br /> <br /> If you white room it, I think the Beast has a slight edge here- primarily because he will try to force the Kuruth, and then play keep away with him. Once the Rage ends, the wolf is helpless. Granted, surviving 10 minutes is a long time, but with a lair trait in play, you could lair hop out, then come back when the hard part is over. An Alternative tactic the beast can use is to enhance his grappling capacity and attempt to pin the raging wolf- but that's really not easy, especially since the werewolf wants to be up close and personal.<br /> <br /> ***<br /> <br /> If I wanted to really work this out, I'd need to build 6 of each splat- a stand alone who is well rounded in all arenas, and 5 'group' members who would fight together and can afford to specialize more. Each of these would be built base at 0xp, then have tiers of say, 15, 30, and 50 xp, where each character is saved in multiple sheets. Each tier, both 1v1 and as a group, would fight 4 matches- One that is a stand up fight, one as hunted, and one as hunter. The final bout would be a purely social manipulation scheme. A lot of work, but with an interesting pay off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8122,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","user":"ArchonAres","date":". 08-24-2017, 05:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T16:42:05-07:00","id":1133583,"title":"","content":"People always goes with the BT Rahu instead of say, the Ithaeur Stormlord immune to Lair traits.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T16:53:50-07:00","id":1133588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1133403-fighting-among-family-beasts-vs-other-splats?p=1133583#post1133583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People always goes with the BT Rahu instead of say, the Ithaeur Stormlord immune to Lair traits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Colour me intrigued! How is the Stormlord immune to Lair traits? Please elaborate!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T17:06:47-07:00","id":1133592,"title":"","content":"Storm Lords aren't automatically immune, but they have an easier time getting the Honor facet of the Gift of Weather which decreases the effects of environmental tilts by the Uratha's Honor. Not sure how applicable that would be on Lair traits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T17:29:27-07:00","id":1133599,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11887_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11887\" data-vbnamecard=\"11887\">Tessie</a> IIRC, traits are considered completely natural, e.g. a Mage's Prime does not help him in avoiding the flames of Burning or the acid of Corrosive (although he might possibly try to dispell the Lair traits themselves? Unsure on that), and the Sunlight of Blazing Light is considered to be just that: really bright sunlight. Not good for Kindred.<br /> However, Suffocating, Stench etc. don't do a thing against Vampires, because they are simply natural things that do natural damage, and a kindred does not need to breath, so not affected.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T18:42:20-07:00","id":1133620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1133403-fighting-among-family-beasts-vs-other-splats?p=1133599#post1133599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11887_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11887\" data-vbnamecard=\"11887\">Tessie</a> IIRC, traits are considered completely natural, e.g. a Mage's Prime does not help him in avoiding the flames of Burning or the acid of Corrosive (although he might possibly try to dispell the Lair traits themselves? Unsure on that), and the Sunlight of Blazing Light is considered to be just that: really bright sunlight. Not good for Kindred.<br /> However, Suffocating, Stench etc. don't do a thing against Vampires, because they are simply natural things that do natural damage, and a kindred does not need to breath, so not affected.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've had a mage decide he'd counter-spell (unravel) my Needs Must Mark before deciding he was going to scrutinize it for all kinds of info on my Atavisms instead. Presumably, Prime 3 lets you walk around shutting down any power you like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T19:15:54-07:00","id":1133627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1133403-fighting-among-family-beasts-vs-other-splats?p=1133592#post1133592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Storm Lords aren't automatically immune, but they have an easier time getting the Honor facet of the Gift of Weather which decreases the effects of environmental tilts by the Uratha's Honor. Not sure how applicable that would be on Lair traits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also access to Calamity, which outright makes you immune to the paired influence. I mean, if you can literally breath fire, why should it burn you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T20:31:42-07:00","id":1133649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1133403-fighting-among-family-beasts-vs-other-splats?p=1133627#post1133627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also access to Calamity, which outright makes you immune to the paired influence. I mean, if you can literally breath fire, why should it burn you?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because only the inside of your mouth and throat is protected against the fire? Because you breath fire with a certain fire rating, any may still be harmed by higher fire rating/ hotter flames?<br /> Sorry, just wanted to point out that B follows A does not necessarily apply here =P<br /> Resistant to stuff like Extreme Cold/Heat, Thin Air and the majority of the sense-attacking Traits (unless all present) would make them crazy resilient for a Beast to take on, especially with the inborn abilities of regeneration and shapeshifting.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11492_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11492\" data-vbnamecard=\"11492\">Arduras</a><br /> Erm, how? You need to be Prime 4 to unravel, so... No. No unraveling at Prime 3 and counter-spell still is a one-dot attainment to my knowledge. Counterspell would still call for a Clash of Wills, not simply eradicate your ability. Three allows fraying, which weakens your spell, but does not take it apart completely. If he claims he uses Dispel Magic, then <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This spell is not potent enough to dispel an archmage\u2019s spells, and <b>only works against Awakened magic</b>. </div> </div> </div> emphasis mine. Even with Prime 4 Supernal Dispillation, you'd withstand with your highest Arcanum Rating, which Beast core has established as your highest resistance rating.<br /> He uses probably uses <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Prime: Universal Counterspell<br /> An Apprentice of Prime understands the formation of spells and the creation of an Imago well enough to attack it on a direct, metaphysical level, allowing her a great deal more defensive capability. System: <b><u><i>The mage may use Counterspell on any Awakened spell</i></u></b>. <b>The player rolls Gnosis + Prime </b>when the character does not know the Arcanum used, or when this would be a higher dice pool than the appropriate Arcanum. <b>The mage may also spend a point of Mana to Counter a spell\u2019s lowest Arcanum rather than its primary Arcanum.</b> For example, a mage with this Attainment Countering a Fate 4, Space 2 spell may pay a point of Mana to roll the Clash of Wills against Gnosis + Space instead of Gnosis + Fate. </div> </div> </div>Here, your ST would have to improvise a bit, and indeed, him spending Mana to roll against your lowest defense rather than your highest would make sense. IF IT WAS AN AWAKENED SPELL. This is not the case. As this specifically asks for Awakened spells, he cannot use Universal Counterspell against Needs Must, imo.<br /> Btw, does he use 1ed or 2ed? Cause that sounds a lot like 1ed. Which might cause some problems, e.g. your xp cost/power ratios are not compatible.<br /> And we already established that scrutinizing takes some time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","user":"Wormwood","date":". 08-24-2017, 11:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T21:12:54-07:00","id":1133658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1133403-fighting-among-family-beasts-vs-other-splats?p=1133649#post1133649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because only the inside of your mouth and throat is protected against the fire? Because you breath fire with a certain fire rating, any may still be harmed by higher fire rating/ hotter flames?<br /> Sorry, just wanted to point out that B follows A does not necessarily apply here =P<br /> Resistant to stuff like Extreme Cold/Heat, Thin Air and the majority of the sense-attacking Traits (unless all present) would make them crazy resilient for a Beast to take on, especially with the inborn abilities of regeneration and shapeshifting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was being poetic, but yes, Storm Lords are resilient as fuck. That's their whole deal. They have to be in order to outlast their sacred prey.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T23:39:13-07:00","id":1133683,"title":"","content":"Why would <b>Princesses</b> and Demons fight? Why wouldn't they fight? Beats spread fear, Princesses fight fear. Beasts encourage their kin to be more monsterous, Princesses encourage monsters to be more humane. Beasts teach lessons drawn from the primordial, Princesses teach lessons drawn from civilisation. A Begotten and a Noble are like two politicians from rival political parties, they disagree on most things, and the things they agree on are even more reason to fight.<br /> <br /> In battle Beasts should favour Nightmares, a Princess' magic is emotional in nature and so Nightmares that attack her emotional stability or self-confidence can be devistating. In a physical bout Princesses usually focus on the simple but scarily effective tactic of manifesting a magical sword or wand of fireballs while pumping up their attributes and skills to superhuman levels. Unless a Beast has some way to land a blow on an opponent with a base Defence of ten (which even applies to guns) or more he'll need some kind of edge. Lair Traits like Cramped or Darkness can even the odds.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Genisues</b> are mad. When a Beast encourages a vampire or a werewolf to indulge his monsterous nature he knows what he's going to get. But who knows what will happen when a Genius abandons self-restraint and gives into his Inspiration? A Beast may be perfectly comfortable encouraging a bit of medical research on orphans only to realise that they've pushed their kin to brew appocolyptic bio-weapons in the basement and now somebody has to take them down quickly. For a Genius' part there's infinite reasons to oppose a Beast once you stop limiting yourself to sane justifications. What does family and friendship matter when your equations prove a Beast is a net harm to humanity? An encouragement to delve deeper implies disagreement with your current actions, and when you alone are smart enough to see the truth the only people who could disagree with you are lesser minds driven to jealousy and spite by your brilliance. Or perhaps the Genius just wants to cut the horror open and document what he finds for science.<br /> <br /> Geniuses embody everything a Beast is not. Their powers come from science and modinanity, however warped. Their insanity derives not from the primordial lizard brain, but from glitches in the brains highest functions: logic, pattern matching, creativity. Consiquentually a Genius can be a devistating threat to a Beast, they are perhaps the only Splat who turn a Lair from an advantage into a weakness. A Genius who builds a nuclear bomb in his basement cannot actually use it without making enemies of everyone, including more powerful geniuses who're quite willing to hop into the time machine and erase his crimes from history. But a detonating that bomb inside a Lair won't attract much attention. An experienced Genius with money and a few weeks of lab time to prepare appropriate tools is an almost unbeatable foe (unless their own insanity trips them up).<br /> <br /> A Beast's best bet then, is to catch their opponent outside their 50 foot attack robot. Without their gadgets a Genius is just a very smart yet crazy human. Chances are the Beast could beat them in a fist fight even without Atavisms. Just about any Avavism or Lair Trait could be useful, what matters is if the Genius has prepared for it and built a specific device to counter it; not what the power does.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Leviathans</b> are demigods. Nobody wins by unfurling their claws, flairing their crest, and picking a fight with Cthulhu. Even a 0 exp Leviathan could have Claws that do seven aggravated damage and a bullet proof armoured hide. At their apex a Leviathan could unleash thousands of zerglings, flood entire cities, and push over skyscrapers. Leviathans aren't outright immune to mental attacks like Nightmares, but they're so hard to affect that they might as well be. <br /> <br /> Why then would a Beast pick a fight with something so powerful? Perhaps the Beast wants to be the apex, ordinary monsters cannot hope to make a bigger impression than a mile wide psychic broadcast screaming &quot;fear and worship me!&quot; into peoples souls. Perhaps the Beast has found there is a limit to their tolerence for a family's monsterousness. A Ravager who fed by throwing a town's local politics into chaos may still feel revulsion at someone forcing the entire population of the town to slaughter each other.<br /> <br /> But more likely is that the Beast dosn't want to fight. Leviathans claim descent from Tiamat, Beasts from the Dark Mother. Is there a connection there? Perhaps, but it is not wise to suggest the possibility to a short tempered religious fanatic. And when Leviathans aren't short tempered and lacking in impulse control, and sometimes even when they are, they're sadistic masterminds who might see a Beast as a useful pawn. A Beast who sees a secluded lake not far from town as a good spot for a Chamber might wake up one day and discover it's advantages were equally appealing to a Leviathan. Worst of all, a Leviathans protection from anything that affects their mind or emotions means that a Beast cannot rely on making a good first impression so simply going to visit the new kin in town is a risk.<br /> <br /> If the fight starts the best strategy for a Beast would be to catch the Leviathan in human form and kill it before it can transform. Failing that simply get out of town and wait for the Leviathans sheer metaphysical size to get it into trouble. Even for a Leviathan, there is always a bigger fish.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T00:50:19-07:00","id":1133698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1133403-fighting-among-family-beasts-vs-other-splats?p=1133683#post1133683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would <b>Princesses</b> and Demons fight? Why wouldn't they fight? Beats spread fear, Princesses fight fear. Beasts encourage their kin to be more monsterous, Princesses encourage monsters to be more humane. Beasts teach lessons drawn from the primordial, Princesses teach lessons drawn from civilisation. A Begotten and a Noble are like two politicians from rival political parties, they disagree on most things, and the things they agree on are even more reason to fight.<br /> <br /> In battle Beasts should favour Nightmares, a Princess' magic is emotional in nature and so Nightmares that attack her emotional stability or self-confidence can be devistating. In a physical bout Princesses usually focus on the simple but scarily effective tactic of manifesting a magical sword or wand of fireballs while pumping up their attributes and skills to superhuman levels. Unless a Beast has some way to land a blow on an opponent with a base Defence of ten (which even applies to guns) or more he'll need some kind of edge. Lair Traits like Cramped or Darkness can even the odds.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Huh. Curious. Might need to take a look at those.<br /> But yeah, actually they have something that might help: Monster from the Deep helps with decreasing the enemies Defense by Lair or outright ignoring it, and Looming Presence gives something like defense in Lair (something like because it is not outright defense, and thus not affected by things that give up or ignore defense - Lair 5 Beast with Looming Presence and Low Satiety can make All-Out Attacks and still reduce incoming attacks by 5 dice).<br /> <br /> Genius are pretty similar to Mages, then.<br /> <br /> Leviathans sound crazy powerful. Especially stuff like 7 Agg Claws at 0 xp. What's their drawback?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T03:16:13-07:00","id":1133716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1133403-fighting-among-family-beasts-vs-other-splats?p=1133698#post1133698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Huh. Curious. Might need to take a look at those.<br /> But yeah, actually they have something that might help: Monster from the Deep helps with decreasing the enemies Defense by Lair or outright ignoring it, and Looming Presence gives something like defense in Lair (something like because it is not outright defense, and thus not affected by things that give up or ignore defense - Lair 5 Beast with Looming Presence and Low Satiety can make All-Out Attacks and still reduce incoming attacks by 5 dice).<br /> <br /> Genius are pretty similar to Mages, then.<br /> <br /> Leviathans sound crazy powerful. Especially stuff like 7 Agg Claws at 0 xp. What's their drawback?</div> </div> </div> </div>They take aggravated damage which their powers can't defend against from electricity and they tend towards insanity. Also, they have cults which can be used against them. That said, they're very, very difficult to fight head-on. Their primary enemies, the Marduk Society, have orbital lightning-shooting magi/clarketech killsats.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T03:19:59-07:00","id":1133717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1133403-fighting-among-family-beasts-vs-other-splats?p=1133698#post1133698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Leviathans sound crazy powerful. Especially stuff like 7 Agg Claws at 0 xp. What's their drawback?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ramping up to Depth 7 is going to take awhile to do safely (spending too much Ichor to speed Transformation can drive them crazy). At Depth 7, they need to be in water or start losing Ichor. They are also a giant mind-bending abomination of the natural order, and prone to make enemies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T03:20:45-07:00","id":1133718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1133403-fighting-among-family-beasts-vs-other-splats?p=1133583#post1133583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People always goes with the BT Rahu instead of say, the Ithaeur Stormlord immune to Lair traits.</div> </div> </div> </div>I chose the most direct to combat approach. Same with anakim.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T06:10:10-07:00","id":1133759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1133403-fighting-among-family-beasts-vs-other-splats?p=1133716#post1133716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They take aggravated damage which their powers can't defend against from electricity and they tend towards insanity. Also, they have cults which can be used against them. That said, they're very, very difficult to fight head-on. Their primary enemies, the Marduk Society, have orbital lightning-shooting magi/clarketech killsats.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh. That's okay then - Storm-Lashed can provide Electricity, as does Electrified. But yeah, they sound like a pain to fight directly.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7212_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7212\" data-vbnamecard=\"7212\">Vent0</a> That does sound better =D","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T10:37:04-07:00","id":1133851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1133403-fighting-among-family-beasts-vs-other-splats?p=1133649#post1133649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because only the inside of your mouth and throat is protected against the fire? Because you breath fire with a certain fire rating, any may still be harmed by higher fire rating/ hotter flames?<br /> Sorry, just wanted to point out that B follows A does not necessarily apply here =P<br /> Resistant to stuff like Extreme Cold/Heat, Thin Air and the majority of the sense-attacking Traits (unless all present) would make them crazy resilient for a Beast to take on, especially with the inborn abilities of regeneration and shapeshifting.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11492_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11492\" data-vbnamecard=\"11492\">Arduras</a><br /> Erm, how? You need to be Prime 4 to unravel, so... No. No unraveling at Prime 3 and counter-spell still is a one-dot attainment to my knowledge. Counterspell would still call for a Clash of Wills, not simply eradicate your ability. Three allows fraying, which weakens your spell, but does not take it apart completely. If he claims he uses Dispel Magic, then emphasis mine. Even with Prime 4 Supernal Dispillation, you'd withstand with your highest Arcanum Rating, which Beast core has established as your highest resistance rating.<br /> He uses probably uses<br /> Here, your ST would have to improvise a bit, and indeed, him spending Mana to roll against your lowest defense rather than your highest would make sense. IF IT WAS AN AWAKENED SPELL. This is not the case. As this specifically asks for Awakened spells, he cannot use Universal Counterspell against Needs Must, imo.<br /> Btw, does he use 1ed or 2ed? Cause that sounds a lot like 1ed. Which might cause some problems, e.g. your xp cost/power ratios are not compatible.<br /> And we already established that scrutinizing takes some time.</div> </div> </div> </div>He thinks like it's 1ed I guess. Death being able to do all sorts of nasty things to vampires, Prime countering just about any supernatural effect, and so on? Where are the rules for unravelling? They've ignored using my Resistance Trait for &quot;Arcanum&quot; and said it only applies to Clash of Wills, which I don't think I agree with. It may &quot;just be a stand in for Clash of Wills&quot; as one has said, but that's really neutering a beast if a mage with half decent prime can just straight up erase effects ala the abjuration discipline just by constantly unraveling over and over. Oh, I see it's a practice. He's just saying spells = all things :/","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","user":"Arduras","date":". 08-25-2017, 01:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T10:58:19-07:00","id":1133860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arduras</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1133403-fighting-among-family-beasts-vs-other-splats?p=1133851#post1133851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> He thinks like it's 1ed I guess. Death being able to do all sorts of nasty things to vampires, Prime countering just about any supernatural effect, and so on? Where are the rules for unravelling? They've ignored using my Resistance Trait for &quot;Arcanum&quot; and said it only applies to Clash of Wills, which I don't think I agree with. It may &quot;just be a stand in for Clash of Wills&quot; as one has said, but that's really neutering a beast if a mage with half decent prime can just straight up erase effects ala the abjuration discipline just by constantly unraveling over and over. Oh, I see it's a practice. He's just saying spells = all things :/</div> </div> </div> </div>Note: Prime's purview is supernal magic, even in 1e. The attainments like counterspell specifically care only about spells.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T13:56:50-07:00","id":1133938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1133403-fighting-among-family-beasts-vs-other-splats?p=1133698#post1133698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Monster from the Deep helps with decreasing the enemies Defense by Lair or outright ignoring it</div> </div> </div> </div> Hmmm. How do Mages with Defence boosting Mage Armour interact with that? It sounds a Clash of Wills should be involved here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1133403-fighting-among-family-beasts-vs-other-splats?p=1133698#post1133698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Genius are pretty similar to Mages, then.</div> </div> </div> </div> In some respects. I'd say that in terms of raw power a Genius can outdo a mage, but Mages win in flexibility hands down. Geniuses need time (and money) to build the good stuff, they can improvise on the scene but it's harder and riskier than mages improvised magic.<br /> <br /> In other respects though Mages and Geniuses are complete opposites. Not so much in a science vs magic sense; this is mad science after all (and Genius is well aware of the fact the mad scientist trope directly descends from the mad aclcheist trope via Victor Frankenstein himself, mechanically you can just say that instead of a death ray you're brewing greek fire). But rather Mage is a game about being powerful, Genius is a game about the world being too big and chaotic for anyone no matter how &quot;powerful&quot; to have any meingful control.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1133403-fighting-among-family-beasts-vs-other-splats?p=1133698#post1133698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Leviathans sound crazy powerful. Especially stuff like 7 Agg Claws at 0 xp. What's their drawback?</div> </div> </div> </div>Their drawback is that they're pretty much stuck babysitting frothing at the mouth lovecraftian cultists for the rest of their lives. If they don't (and often even when they do) those cultists will break the masqurade through incompetence or sometimes deliberately preaching in public and attract the attention of enemies who are perfectly capable of taking down a Leviathan.<br /> <br /> They also have worse psychological problems than Vampires, a vulnerability to electricity, and need time to transform into an obviously inhuman form before they can unlock their powers.<br /> <br /> Finally while Leviathans are extreemly good at combat and dominating others; they don't get much supernatural advantages to do anything you might actually want to do: Healing, building stuff, earning an honest living.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1133403-fighting-among-family-beasts-vs-other-splats?p=1133759#post1133759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh. That's okay then - Storm-Lashed can provide Electricity, as does Electrified. But yeah, they sound like a pain to fight directly.</div> </div> </div> </div>I totally missed Storm-Lashed and Electrified <img src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> But even with Storm-Lashed simply attacking a Leviathan is not a good idea. In terms of design Leviathans are more like the evil god you have to stop the actual antagonist from summoning than the antagonist. Or they're like the zombies in a zombie series - the real antagonists are humans, the zombies/sleeping leviathan just provide an excuse for society to break down and humans to go crazy. They're too powerful for most protagonists to fight directly, but they can be defeated through the use of McGuffins.<br /> <br /> The Rituals rules were actually specifically balanced so a Leviathan could do something weird to an entire town but leave the player characters unaffected.<br /> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\">Save</span></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 08-25-2017, 05:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-29T09:44:09-07:00","id":1145265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1133403-fighting-among-family-beasts-vs-other-splats?p=1133938#post1133938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Hmmm. How do Mages with Defence boosting Mage Armour interact with that? It sounds a Clash of Wills should be involved here.<br /> <br /> They also have worse psychological problems than Vampires, a vulnerability to electricity, and need time to transform into an obviously inhuman form before they can unlock their powers.<br /> <br /> Finally while Leviathans are extreemly good at combat and dominating others; they don't get much supernatural advantages to do anything you might actually want to do: Healing, building stuff, earning an honest living.<br /> <br /> I totally missed Storm-Lashed and Electrified <img src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> But even with Storm-Lashed simply attacking a Leviathan is not a good idea. In terms of design Leviathans are more like the evil god you have to stop the actual antagonist from summoning than the antagonist. Or they're like the zombies in a zombie series - the real antagonists are humans, the zombies/sleeping leviathan just provide an excuse for society to break down and humans to go crazy. They're too powerful for most protagonists to fight directly, but they can be defeated through the use of McGuffins.<br /> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\">Save</span></div></div> </div> </div> </div>Clah of wills COULD be done, but honestly, I wouldn't bother and just apply both. I mean, one gives you more defense, the other reduces your defense. I don't see a need for a CoW, as you can let both apply, and both do exactly what they are meant to do (the mage still benefits by having more defense than if he hadn't used the spell, the Beast still benefits from having to fight against lower defense than he would have to otherwise). As for the &quot;outright ignoring&quot;: that is a dodgeable (for Supernaturals) attack against which defense does not apply and which costs one Satiety, so I would not call for a CoW (defence-boosting armor does not help you reducing the damage of a bomb, either. Furthermore, higher defense means higher Dodge dice pool, so both still benefit enough from their abilities to have them apply at the same time imo).<br /> <br /> Also, sounds to me like a starting beast could indeed take down a Leviathan, although with carefully chosen abilities.Storm-Lashed and Shadow-Souled for Atavisms and Electrified as well as Crosswind(or Downpour, or Blizzard, or.... any Storm-related minor trait, really) as a Lair Trait, use Sat-expenditure to create a storm, use the winds to call down Electrified, vanish into the shadows (potentially spending Satiety) and let the abilities whittle down at the enemy (in fact, low Satiety Beasts could use Lightning bolts from the safety of the shadows rather than/in addition to Electrified). Would not be easy, but certainly possible. Beasts with a bit of Lair (e.g. Merit points spend on Lair, so the creation char has Lair 3) as well as Cyclopean Strenght and Limb From Limb are not slouches, either: spent one Satiety on Cyclopean Strength + one per every attack on Limb from Limb, deal 6+Successes Aggravated per attack. Huh. Rather close to the 7 Agg example.<br /> Basilisk's Touch and From the Shadows are probably the strongest combination at whittling targets down. Surprise touch attack, vanish, wait, repeat.<br /> <br /> So yeah, Leviathans are obviously tough, but I think a determined enough Beast could do it, even if it is by whittling them down. Same as Werewolves: freaking scary enemies, but can be put down with the right tools/tactics.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-29T11:12:42-07:00","id":1145306,"title":"","content":"There's an even better way for a Beast to kill a leviathan. Take From the Darkness and use that stealth to assassinate the Leviathan in human form. It's risky if the Leviathan has a way to contest invisibility, but it's less risky than trying to stay hidden while the Lair wittles the Leviathan down for you. That has the advantage of being viable against high level Leviathans since if they're in human form they're not the size of Godzilla.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-08T23:26:40-07:00","id":1148230,"title":"","content":"I have a much more simpler answer to why the Supernatural Community might come into conflict with Beasts, one in which both the most humane (the ones who still identify with their Life and actively try to minimize the damage done by their Legend and Hunger) and heinous (the Strix kinship making mother f$&amp;kers) of Begotten might qualify: Beasts are the ultimate interlopers. <br /> <br /> They can practically go anywhere. Some can tell exactly where you are at all times if they've seen you once. Some can know your dreams, desires, or darkest secrets just with a glance. They seem to attract a lot of unwanted attention, especially from glory hounds that seem to possess supernatural powers against them and those they come into close or continual contact with. And they prefer to not take a side when they can. What the hell is up with them? What do they truly want? Where did they come from? Are we really descendants from their Dark Mother? Or are they just nightmares born of the humans we prey upon? And most importantly why do they keep watching me while I feed! Go away asshole! This is me time, I don't care if you think we're cousins! Wait, are those photos? What have you seen?! Who have you spoken to!?!?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-11T00:19:07-07:00","id":1148767,"title":"","content":"Does anyone have any idea of what kind of relationship (primarily negative, but positives are always good) Beasts would have with Sirens? (A fan-splat, I know, but still full of an incredible amount of possibility.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10141-solaris","name":"Solaris","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10141_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}